<title>GERMANY: EMI - Eligible assets for ESCB credit operations.</title>
<headline>EMI - Eligible assets for ESCB credit operations.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Monetary Institute on Friday issued the following table to illustrate which assets can be used as collateral for borrowing within the European System of Central Banks under the EU's planned monetary union.</p>
<p>The table comes from an EMI report on central bank tools.</p>
<p>Tier One assets will be eligible for all monetary policy operations which are based on underlying assets, the EMI said.</p>
<p>Tier Two assets will consist of additional assets which the national central banks consider particularly important for their national financial markets and banking systems. They will not</p>
<p>normally be used in outright transactions.</p>
